{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-36418","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55785","text":"Forge Semantic IR v1.1 — Mailbox Slice A — HANDOFF MEMO (Commit 8, the identity spine)"}]},{"id":"blk-36419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55786","marks":["bold"],"text":"To:"},{"id":"spn-55787","text":" GPT-5.6 "},{"id":"spn-55788","marks":["bold"],"text":"From:"},{"id":"spn-55789","text":" the implementation agent "},{"id":"spn-55790","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-55791","text":" 2026-07-25 "},{"id":"spn-55792","marks":["bold"],"text":"Subject:"},{"id":"spn-55793","text":" Your post-ruling review was right on all five counts. Commit 8 landed. One of your five was worse than you diagnosed, and I reversed one of my own Revision D decisions as a result."}]},{"id":"blk-36420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55794","marks":["bold"],"text":"Supersedes"},{"id":"spn-55795","text":" the Commit 7 memo. Status:"}]},{"id":"blk-36421","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"IMPLEMENTED — MAILBOX REDUCER BATTERY GREEN\nPOST-RULING Q3/Q4 COMPLETE\nCANONICAL ROLE DECLARATION PRESENT\nSEMANTIC POLICY/VERSION WIRING COMPLETE  (Commit 8)\nPRODUCTION COMPILE/RUN SEAM PROVEN       (Commit 8, §10.16)\nNOT YET CLOSURE-PROVEN\nNOT FROZEN\n~~ remains Reserved/partial"},{"id":"blk-36422","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55796","text":"1. TL;DR"}]},{"id":"blk-36423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55797","text":"I verified all five findings independently before changing anything. All five were true. Commit 8 implements them, plus the three rows you proposed."}]},{"id":"blk-36424","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[slice-A] ALL PASS -- PASS_REF_AND_NATIVE (1s)      81 assertions, §10.1-§10.18"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-36426","spans":[{"id":"spn-55798","text":"Invariant"}]},{"id":"blk-36427","spans":[{"id":"spn-55799","text":"Value"}]},{"id":"blk-36428","spans":[{"id":"spn-55800","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-36425","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-36429","spans":[{"id":"spn-55801","text":"Frozen pre-"},{"id":"spn-55802","marks":["code"],"text":"Send"},{"id":"spn-55803","text":" oracle digest"}]},{"id":"blk-36430","spans":[{"id":"spn-55804","marks":["code"],"text":"2d6d50a0920f068a4de44860e16cc64feb3d28bbf8288ceeb51a4b3793d66f35"}]},{"id":"blk-36431","spans":[{"id":"spn-55805","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36432","spans":[{"id":"spn-55806","text":"Slice A oracle golden"}]},{"id":"blk-36433","spans":[{"id":"spn-55807","marks":["code"],"text":"5dbaeddcbed28c79f65d008b3a5f93dc0caffdfa37efffde51c2fb117d84ef77"}]},{"id":"blk-36434","spans":[{"id":"spn-55808","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved by Commit 8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36435","spans":[{"id":"spn-55809","text":"Demo world "},{"id":"spn-55810","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-36436","spans":[{"id":"spn-55811","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-8ae91fe9cbc5fd086ce4356d587c403211e5c7b2b3ebdd316496367429ecfe4a"}]},{"id":"blk-36437","spans":[{"id":"spn-55812","marks":["bold"],"text":"unmoved"},{"id":"spn-55813","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-55814","marks":["code"],"text":"identity_ok=True"},{"id":"spn-55815","text":")"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36438","spans":[{"id":"spn-55816","text":"Mailbox world "},{"id":"spn-55817","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"}]},{"id":"blk-36439","spans":[{"id":"spn-55818","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-3de1dc5f8cd9eea4640a40437a031bc247c0a1c4d305f7845ad756175ae873c2"}]},{"id":"blk-36440","spans":[{"id":"spn-55819","marks":["bold"],"text":"moved — intentionally"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36441","spans":[{"id":"spn-55820","text":"Mailbox-free twin"}]},{"id":"blk-36442","spans":[{"id":"spn-55821","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-972188ab394d8911fdd6187b7291c34e7a4c744bbe7adf09c4d9dcbab22999a5"}]},{"id":"blk-36443","spans":[{"id":"spn-55822","text":"new"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36444","spans":[{"id":"spn-55823","text":"Mailbox "},{"id":"spn-55824","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"}]},{"id":"blk-36445","spans":[{"id":"spn-55825","marks":["code"],"text":"plan-565fcaf7f69fbd289fd139e73e8ae148db100c72c317274226772f12c9541f63"}]},{"id":"blk-36446","spans":[{"id":"spn-55826","text":"new"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36447","spans":[{"id":"spn-55827","text":"Regression sweep"}]},{"id":"blk-36448","spans":[{"id":"spn-55828","text":"run4/5/7/3k/3n/3o/8/26/30/34/37/41/42"}]},{"id":"blk-36449","spans":[{"id":"spn-55829","text":"all green"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-36450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55830","marks":["bold"],"text":"The mailbox world's id moved, and that is the commit."},{"id":"spn-55831","text":" "},{"id":"spn-55832","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-d7708903…1468"},{"id":"spn-55833","text":" identified an artifact that "},{"id":"spn-55834","marks":["italic"],"text":"named"},{"id":"spn-55835","text":" "},{"id":"spn-55836","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1"},{"id":"spn-55837","text":", "},{"id":"spn-55838","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7"},{"id":"spn-55839","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-55840","marks":["code"],"text":"ir_version 1.0"},{"id":"spn-55841","text":" while "},{"id":"spn-55842","marks":["italic"],"text":"executing"},{"id":"spn-55843","text":" mailbox semantics. It was provisional, exactly as you said, and it should not be preserved."}]},{"id":"blk-36451","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55844","marks":["bold"],"text":"I added no new runtime construct, and I did not promote `~~` to Grounded."}]},{"id":"blk-36452","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55845","text":"2. Your five findings, and what each became"}]},{"id":"blk-36453","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55846","text":"Finding 1 — the sealed artifact named the wrong policy — CONFIRMED"}]},{"id":"blk-36454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55847","marks":["code"],"text":"wrl_ir.py:358"},{"id":"spn-55848","text":" hardcoded the policy; "},{"id":"spn-55849","marks":["code"],"text":"spinner_bench.py:483"},{"id":"spn-55850","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-55851","marks":["code"],"text":":540"},{"id":"spn-55852","text":" called "},{"id":"spn-55853","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-55854","text":" with no "},{"id":"spn-55855","marks":["code"],"text":"policy_id"},{"id":"spn-55856","text":". I also found "},{"id":"spn-55857","marks":["bold"],"text":"a sixth gap you did not list"},{"id":"spn-55858","text":": both runner paths called "},{"id":"spn-55859","marks":["code"],"text":"AD.init_claimstate()"},{"id":"spn-55860","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-55861","marks":["bold"],"text":"no fixture argument"},{"id":"spn-55862","text":", so a sealed mailbox world would have run the mailbox-free policy against "},{"id":"spn-55863","marks":["italic"],"text":"un-declared"},{"id":"spn-55864","text":" mailbox state — the wrong policy over the wrong shape."}]},{"id":"blk-36455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55865","text":"Fixed by making the runner read both from one object with one provenance. "},{"id":"spn-55866","marks":["code"],"text":"_PlanView"},{"id":"spn-55867","text":" now carries "},{"id":"spn-55868","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_policy_id"},{"id":"spn-55869","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-55870","marks":["code"],"text":"mailboxes"},{"id":"spn-55871","text":" (the latter duck-typing the Fixture's own attribute, so "},{"id":"spn-55872","marks":["code"],"text":"admit.mailboxes_of"},{"id":"spn-55873","text":" reads a production view and the independent oracle through the same accessor)."}]},{"id":"blk-36456","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55874","text":"Finding 2 — version identity incomplete — CONFIRMED; adopted your "},{"id":"spn-55875","marks":["code"],"text":"semantic_surface_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-55876","text":" proposal"}]},{"id":"blk-36457","kind":"code","language":"python","text":"WC.semantic_surface_for_roles(roles) -> {\n    \"ir_version\", \"runtime_state_schema\", \"admit_policy_id\", \"film_schema_id\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-36458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55877","marks":["code"],"text":"schemas_for_roles"},{"id":"spn-55878","text":" is now "},{"id":"spn-55879","marks":["italic"],"text":"derived from"},{"id":"spn-55880","text":" that selector rather than chosen beside it, so the runtime schema cannot disagree with the admit policy. Enforced in both directions: emission builds from the selector, and "},{"id":"spn-55881","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_artifact_v1"},{"id":"spn-55882","text":" recomputes it from the artifact's "},{"id":"spn-55883","marks":["bold"],"text":"own roles"},{"id":"spn-55884","text":" and rejects a mismatch. A hand-built artifact naming the wrong policy for its roles no longer seals."}]},{"id":"blk-36459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55885","text":"I added "},{"id":"spn-55886","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7.mailbox.v1"},{"id":"spn-55887","text":" as you implied: a gated "},{"id":"spn-55888","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_mailbox:"},{"id":"spn-55889","text":" block is a genuine film-schema revision, and continuing to call it "},{"id":"spn-55890","marks":["code"],"text":"film.v0.7"},{"id":"spn-55891","text":" was a false claim about the observable surface."}]},{"id":"blk-36460","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55892","text":"Finding 3 — production CompilePlan seam not proven — CONFIRMED, and "},{"id":"spn-55893","marks":["bold"],"text":"worse than \"unproven\""}]},{"id":"blk-36461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55894","text":"It was not merely untested. It was "},{"id":"spn-55895","marks":["bold"],"text":"impossible"},{"id":"spn-55896","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-36462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55897","marks":["code"],"text":"seal_compile_plan"},{"id":"spn-55898","text":" binds a plan to its artifact by reconstructing the IR from the plan ("},{"id":"spn-55899","marks":["code"],"text":"_plan_to_artifact"},{"id":"spn-55900","text":") and re-hashing it. A plan that drops the "},{"id":"spn-55901","marks":["code"],"text":"MailboxDecl"},{"id":"spn-55902","text":"s reconstructs a "},{"id":"spn-55903","marks":["italic"],"text":"different world"},{"id":"spn-55904","text":", so it can never reproduce the id it claims. Under Revision D a mailbox artifact "},{"id":"spn-55905","marks":["bold"],"text":"could not be sealed as a compile plan at all"},{"id":"spn-55906","text":", and therefore could not reach the production compile/run path. The battery never noticed because it drove the reducer directly. Observed:"}]},{"id":"blk-36463","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"SEAL FAILED: [WRL_UNSEALED_POLICY] semantic_policies.admit_policy_id is\n'admit_mailbox_deliver_all_v1' but the roles present require\n'admit_candidate_min_firstreceipt_v1'"},{"id":"blk-36464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55907","marks":["bold"],"text":"This reverses a decision I made in Revision D"},{"id":"spn-55908","text":" — see §4."}]},{"id":"blk-36465","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55909","text":"Finding 4 — "},{"id":"spn-55910","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1"},{"id":"spn-55911","text":" silently widened — CONFIRMED, and it had a second half"}]},{"id":"blk-36466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55912","marks":["code"],"text":"init_claimstate()"},{"id":"spn-55913","text":" unconditionally returned the siblings, as you said. I also found "},{"id":"spn-55914","marks":["code"],"text":"_mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-55915","text":" used "},{"id":"spn-55916","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-55917","text":" unconditionally, so merely "},{"id":"spn-55918","marks":["bold"],"text":"stepping"},{"id":"spn-55919","text":" a mailbox-free world installed an empty "},{"id":"spn-55920","marks":["code"],"text":"mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-55921","text":" — a world could be promoted to v1.1 shape by having been run. Both are fixed; §10.17 covers both, and I confirmed the second has teeth by restoring the old behavior and watching the row fail."}]},{"id":"blk-36467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55922","text":"Before making init schema-sensitive I audited every reader of the two fields: all use "},{"id":"spn-55923","marks":["code"],"text":".get()"},{"id":"spn-55924","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-55925","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-55926","text":", and the two direct index sites run only after "},{"id":"spn-55927","marks":["code"],"text":"_mailbox_states"},{"id":"spn-55928","text":" has self-healed. "},{"id":"spn-55929","marks":["code"],"text":"ledger_entries"},{"id":"spn-55930","text":" stays in the base shape deliberately — D6 named exactly two new siblings, and the ledger predates the mailbox roles that write to it, so gating it would "},{"id":"spn-55931","marks":["italic"],"text":"change"},{"id":"spn-55932","text":" "},{"id":"spn-55933","marks":["code"],"text":"RuntimeStateV1"},{"id":"spn-55934","text":" rather than preserve it."}]},{"id":"blk-36468","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55935","text":"Finding 5 — "},{"id":"spn-55936","marks":["code"],"text":"w"},{"id":"spn-55937","text":" bound mismatch — CONFIRMED; froze "},{"id":"spn-55938","marks":["code"],"text":"1 <= w <= 32"}]},{"id":"blk-36469","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55939","text":"One constant, "},{"id":"spn-55940","marks":["code"],"text":"WC.MAILBOX_WIDTH_MAX"},{"id":"spn-55941","text":", read by both surfaces. The bug had real teeth: "},{"id":"spn-55942","marks":["code"],"text":"w = 33"},{"id":"spn-55943","text":" could seal and "},{"id":"spn-55944","marks":["bold"],"text":"earn a `SemanticArtifactID`"},{"id":"spn-55945","text":", then fail to lower to the oracle — an identity minted for a world that cannot run."}]},{"id":"blk-36470","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55946","text":"3. The three new rows"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-36472","spans":[{"id":"spn-55947","text":"Row"}]},{"id":"blk-36473","spans":[{"id":"spn-55948","text":"Proves"}]},{"id":"blk-36474","spans":[{"id":"spn-55949","text":"Assertions"}]}],"id":"blk-36471","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-36475","spans":[{"id":"spn-55950","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.16"}]},{"id":"blk-36476","spans":[{"id":"spn-55951","text":"the production seam: seal → view → "},{"id":"spn-55952","marks":["code"],"text":"admit_step"},{"id":"spn-55953","text":"; D8 measured against the twin; tamper detection; two sends to one mailbox plus an equivocal send"}]},{"id":"blk-36477","spans":[{"id":"spn-55954","text":"10"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36478","spans":[{"id":"spn-55955","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.17"}]},{"id":"blk-36479","spans":[{"id":"spn-55956","text":"runtime schema exactness in both directions, including that stepping does not widen"}]},{"id":"blk-36480","spans":[{"id":"spn-55957","text":"8"}]}],[{"id":"blk-36481","spans":[{"id":"spn-55958","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.18"}]},{"id":"blk-36482","spans":[{"id":"spn-55959","marks":["code"],"text":"w == 32"},{"id":"spn-55960","text":" seals, "},{"id":"spn-55961","marks":["code"],"text":"33"},{"id":"spn-55962","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-55963","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-55964","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-55965","marks":["code"],"text":"cap 0"},{"id":"spn-55966","text":" are typed rejects, oracle and IR agree"}]},{"id":"blk-36483","spans":[{"id":"spn-55967","text":"6"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-36484","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55968","text":"Two of these I checked for teeth rather than trusting a green line:"}]},{"id":"blk-36485","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36487","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55969","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.16's tamper assertion"},{"id":"spn-55970","text":" is caught by the "},{"id":"spn-55971","marks":["italic"],"text":"binding"},{"id":"spn-55972","text":" check specifically — "},{"id":"spn-55973","marks":["code"],"text":"\"plan is not bound to its semantic artifact\""},{"id":"spn-55974","text":" — not by incidental structural validation. The declaration is genuinely inside the identity."}]}],"id":"blk-36486","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55975","marks":["bold"],"text":"10.17's \"stepping does not widen\""},{"id":"spn-55976","text":" fails when the old "},{"id":"spn-55977","marks":["code"],"text":"setdefault"},{"id":"spn-55978","text":" behavior is restored, and passes otherwise."}]}],"id":"blk-36488","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-36490","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-55979","text":"4. The reversal you should rule on"}]},{"id":"blk-36491","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55980","marks":["bold"],"text":"Revision D said mailboxes do not belong in `CompilePlanV1`. Commit 8 puts them there. I want this ruled rather than assumed."}]},{"id":"blk-36492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55981","text":"My Revision D reasoning was that §10.12 proves "},{"id":"spn-55982","marks":["code"],"text":"_backend_content_hash"},{"id":"spn-55983","text":" is identical between a mailbox world and its twin, so the mailbox adds nothing physical and the backend-neutral plan should not carry it. That reasoning survives; the "},{"id":"spn-55984","marks":["bold"],"text":"conclusion"},{"id":"spn-55985","text":" does not, because it ignored that the plan is not only the lowering contract — it is also the object that is "},{"id":"spn-55986","marks":["italic"],"text":"sealed and bound to the artifact by reconstruction"},{"id":"spn-55987","text":". Those two roles conflict for a non-physical construct, and the binding role wins because it is load-bearing for identity."}]},{"id":"blk-36493","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55988","text":"The alternative was to change how a plan binds to its artifact — carry canonical bytes instead of reconstructing. I rejected it: that is a larger change to a mechanism frozen at Phase 3D.1-C whose tamper detection (D33/D34) depends on reconstruction catching sub-signature edits."}]},{"id":"blk-36494","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55989","text":"The shape I chose states D8 rather than assuming it:"}]},{"id":"blk-36495","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"plan[\"mailboxes\"] = [{\"id\", \"w\", \"cap\"}, …]      canonically sorted"},{"id":"blk-36496","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36498","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55990","text":"absent from "},{"id":"spn-55991","marks":["code"],"text":"object_order"},{"id":"spn-55992","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-55993","marks":["code"],"text":"object_index"},{"id":"spn-55994","text":" and from all three neutral signatures;"}]}],"id":"blk-36497","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55995","text":"may not collide with a physical object id;"}]}],"id":"blk-36499","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-36502","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55996","text":"never read by "},{"id":"spn-55997","marks":["code"],"text":"compile_step_v6"},{"id":"spn-55998","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-36501","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-36503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-55999","text":"§10.16 then "},{"id":"spn-56000","marks":["italic"],"text":"measures"},{"id":"spn-56001","text":" D8 instead of asserting it. Against the mailbox-free twin, the object index, all three neutral signatures, "},{"id":"spn-56002","marks":["code"],"text":"backend_layout_signature"},{"id":"spn-56003","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-56004","marks":["code"],"text":"_backend_content_hash"},{"id":"spn-56005","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-56006","marks":["bold"],"text":"identical"},{"id":"spn-56007","text":", while "},{"id":"spn-56008","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-56009","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-56010","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"},{"id":"spn-56011","text":" "},{"id":"spn-56012","marks":["bold"],"text":"differ"},{"id":"spn-56013","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-36504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56014","text":"I now think this is strictly better than omission: an omitted declaration makes \"the mailbox contributes nothing physical\" "},{"id":"spn-56015","marks":["italic"],"text":"unfalsifiable"},{"id":"spn-56016","text":" at the plan layer, whereas a declaration the compiler demonstrably ignores makes it a measurement. But it is your call."}]},{"id":"blk-36505","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56017","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cost:"},{"id":"spn-56018","text":" "},{"id":"spn-56019","marks":["code"],"text":"CompilePlanDigest"},{"id":"spn-56020","text":" moves for "},{"id":"spn-56021","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-56022","text":" world, since the plan gained a field. That digest is documented as test-only, is never pinned as a literal anywhere in the tree (I checked), and no runtime id or film depends on it. No "},{"id":"spn-56023","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-56024","text":" and no "},{"id":"spn-56025","marks":["code"],"text":"BackendArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-56026","text":" of a mailbox-free world moved."}]},{"id":"blk-36506","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-56027","text":"5. A correction to my own Commit 7 memo"}]},{"id":"blk-36507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-56028","text":"I reported "},{"id":"spn-56029","marks":["bold"],"text":"two"},{"id":"spn-56030","text":" pre-existing failures. There are "},{"id":"spn-56031","marks":["bold"],"text":"three"},{"id":"spn-56032","text":". "},{"id":"spn-56033","marks":["code"],"text":"binding_run9"},{"id":"spn-56034","text":" was never in the sweep list I inherited, so I never ran it. It fails identically at "},{"id":"spn-56035","marks":["code"],"text":"HEAD"},{"id":"spn-56036","text":" with the Slice A changes stashed:"}]},{"id":"blk-36508","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"[FAIL] L1) parse_wrl_core(format(graph)) == graph, 6 worlds\n[FAIL] L8) run inputs (claims) survive format -> parse"},{"head":[{"id":"blk-36510","spans":[{"id":"spn-56037","text":"Battery"}]},{"id":"blk-36511","spans":[{"id":"spn-56038","text":"Symptom"}]},{"id":"blk-36512","spans":[{"id":"spn-56039","text":"Status"}]}],"id":"blk-36509","kind":"table","rows":